# Content & Blog

Blog posts are MDX files in `contents/blog/`. Frontmatter fields read by the app: `title`, `summary`, `publishedAt`, optional `author` and `imageUrl`. `@next/mdx` compiles each post at build time and exports its YAML frontmatter as `frontmatter`.

Reading utilities live in `src/lib/blog.ts`: `getAllPosts()` returns posts sorted newest-first (used by `src/app/blog/page.tsx` and `src/app/sitemap.ts`); `getPost(slug)` returns `{ metadata, Content }`, `Content` being the compiled post. Both read the posts from the bundle, which `import.meta.glob('/contents/blog/*.mdx', { eager: true })` fills at build time, never from the filesystem: a Cloudflare Worker has no `contents/` directory, so a `fs` read in a page, in `generateMetadata` or in `blog.ts` fails there even though `next build` passes. Keep the `contents/blog/` directory.

The post route `src/app/blog/[slug]/page.tsx` calls `generateStaticParams()` from `getAllPosts()`, sets `dynamicParams = false` (any other slug is a 404), renders `<post.Content />` (components from `src/mdx-components.tsx`), and emits `ArticleJsonLd` plus `Breadcrumbs`.

## Persona pages
Persona data lives in `src/lib/data/personas.ts` (`slug`, `title`, `headline`, `description`, `benefits[]`, `faq[]`). `src/app/for/[persona]/page.tsx` statically generates one page per `getAllPersonaSlugs()`, sets `dynamicParams = false` (any other slug is a 404, in `dev` too) and emits `FaqJsonLd` from the persona's `faq`.

## Adding a blog post
1. Create `contents/blog/my-post.mdx` with `title`, `summary`, `publishedAt` (and optional `author`/`imageUrl`) frontmatter.
2. Write MDX below the frontmatter, starting at `##`: the post page renders `title` as the only `h1`. It is picked up automatically (slug = filename) and added to the sitemap.

## Adding a persona
1. Append a `Persona` object to the `personas` array in `src/lib/data/personas.ts`.
2. The `/for/{slug}` page and sitemap entry are generated automatically.
